\item a \strong{closed} (\code{"sandwich"}) Godambe estimator with an explicit
\code{bread} (\code{H}: inverse MCMC draw covariance, or the negative
Hessian at an MLE or MAP) and an explicit \code{meat} (\code{J}: the score-vector moment
estimator, or a draw-averaged version);
\item an \strong{open-faced} (\code{"ofs"}) sandwich estimator (Shaby, 2014):
the same explicit \code{bread}/\code{meat}, applied as the draw
transform \code{Omega = (Q^-1 P)^(1/2)} without calibrating to the
empirical draw covariance;
\item a \code{ci} type (quantile or Wald);
\item a scalar magnitude (scale) adjustment (\code{magnitude_adjust()}).
}
The legacy \code{methods} presets (\code{noadj}, \code{ijse}, \code{ijse2},
\code{curvadj}, \code{curvadj2}, \code{curvadj3}) remain as silent aliases
